 READING (honest)
==================================================================================================
  * mac-mini PIVOT CONFIRMED: the loose lcm-block is M~0.28 (3.9x the radius), mu=0.108 -- easily lonely,
    NOT the crux. The TIGHT covering families (deep well, random cov) have small mu (R near -1) = the crux.
  * mu = (6/7)^13 + resonances (integer sum m_i v_i = 0); the DANGER BAND's Fourier vanishes at 7|m
    (the heptagon), and the PAIR resonance term ~ g^2/(v_i v_j) is gcd-controlled: commensurate = large g.
  * commensurability (sum gcd^2) POSITIVELY correlates with mu (angle REAL) -- but does NOT close the crux:
    the tight families have R near -1 and sign-delicate pair terms; mu>0 (=M>=1/14=LRC14) is unproven here.
  This is the exact measure-resonance form + the 7/gcd structure feeding the measure route (klein/mac-mini).
